  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.2.0 — Files this library writes are now readable by Microsoft Access, which\n      previously they often were not. Text in a column without unicode compression\n      is no longer written compressed (ASCII came back as CJK-looking nonsense), and\n      a table created here is now visible and readable in Access: catalog rows are\n      parented to the Tables container with access-control entries, multi-column\n      index entries use Jet's per-column framing, column headers carry the running\n      variable-length index and the text sort order, and a table's usage maps live\n      on a data page. Also from 2.0.0: .NET 10 only (net8.0 dropped) and usage-map\n      growth so appending past ~2 MB works. See CHANGELOG.md.",
